nodecode-secret-drop is a rewrite of Goitonthefloor's Goitonthefloor/hermes-secret-drop:

  https://github.com/Goitonthefloor/hermes-secret-drop
  commit 505bd3b47937ae453d4a54a2ee2455a4d274bf42
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 secret-drop contributors (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the command that takes a secret without it entering the
conversation, the store the value lands in, the environment the agent's shell
commands inherit it from, the exact-match redaction of a credential-shaped
value on the way to the model, and the guidance that tells the model to ask for
a drop instead of a paste. The original is Python and a Hermes plugin; this is
Common Lisp and a Nodecode cell, and it makes no network call.

What was left out, and why: the Hermes desktop key button beside the composer
and the dashboard route behind it, because Nodecode's drop is the slash command
and the two tools rather than a second UI; the profile `.env` and
`terminal.env_passthrough` write, because there is no such file to keep in
step here, so the store is the cell's own file and the environment is the one
the image's shell commands already inherit; the per-profile scope of a write,
because a Nodecode process is one profile; and the private Hermes helpers the
original imported to validate a name and to find provider credentials, which
this rewrite writes out itself.
